{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## /rebar-debug — Phase 1: proven root cause (RCA)\n\n**Mechanism (confirmed at runtime).** `infra/compose/Dockerfile.mcp` has no `acli` install step,\nso the built image ships without the Atlassian CLI on `PATH`. The reconciler's Jira transport\nspawns `acli` by **bare name** — `_DEFAULT_ACLI_CMD = [\"acli\"]` in\n`adapters/jira/acli_subprocess.py`, run via `subprocess.Popen(full_cmd, ...)` in `_run_acli`\n(no `shutil.which`/abs-path guard). When the binary is absent, `Popen` raises\n`FileNotFoundError: [Errno 2] No such file or directory: 'acli'`. `bridge_check_access`'s\n`STEP_CREATE` calls `client.create_issue()`, whose `except Exception` arm\n(`access_check.py:237-241`) reports `reason=exception, detail=str(exc)` — surfacing the raw\n`FileNotFoundError` string exactly as observed.\n\n**Discriminating proof.**\n- `grep -rn \"acli\\|atlassian\" infra/compose/Dockerfile.*` → nothing; no image provisions `acli`.\n- Runtime reproduction of the exact error with `acli` off `PATH`:\n  `subprocess.Popen(['acli','--version'], env={'PATH':'/nonexistent'})` →\n  `RAISED: \"[Errno 2] No such file or directory: 'acli'\"` — byte-for-byte the ticket's `detail`.\n- This discriminates against the ruled-out rivals the ticket already excluded: credentials\n  (`GET /rest/api/3/myself` → 200), connectivity, and project scope are all proven good; the\n  failure is specifically the missing `acli` subprocess transport.\n\n**Legitimacy = defect (incomplete-implementation of the image).** The on-box MCP server the image\nhosts is *designed* to drive the Jira-mutating bridge (`bridge_check_access`, `reconcile`; ADR\n0104 / `docs/adr/0104-mcp-on-box.md`), and `acli` is an already-accepted, load-bearing, **pinned**\nrebar dependency — README §tools, `docs/jira-sync-setup.md` (`ACLI_VERSION=1.3.19-stable` +\n`ACLI_SHA256`), and CI `.github/workflows/external-integration.yml` (download + sha256-verify +\ninstall onto PATH). The image build simply omits the install step CI already performs.\n\n**Escalation resolved → mechanical fix, NOT a new-dependency decision.** `acli` is public, free\n(no license/account — both arch tarballs downloaded anonymously), single ~15 MB static binary in a\n~6 MB tarball, pinnable to `1.3.19-stable` with per-arch sha256. It is not a new external\ndependency; it is one already declared and pinned elsewhere in the repo. Per /rebar-debug Step 5\nthis is the \"already-accepted dependency the image omits\" case → proceed, no unilateral adoption.\n\n**Portability + arch caveat.** The deploy box is **AL2023 arm64** (`docker-compose.yml:4`), but CI\ndownloads the **amd64** tarball. A naive copy of the CI amd64 install would ship a non-executable\nbinary on the arm64 box. The image install therefore selects the arch via Docker's `TARGETARCH`\nand pins a per-arch sha256 (amd64 `f29fa8b7…383a6d`, arm64 `72972e74…3674da` for `1.3.19-stable`).\nThe fix is a plain Dockerfile build step (no CI/deploy-system coupling), so it satisfies\n`project.portability`.\n\n**Defect origin (`caused_by`).** Commit `8297083532a3` \"Add rebar-mcp HTTP service to the AWS box\"\n(ticket `fd4a-4e91-f179-4932`) introduced `Dockerfile.mcp` for the on-box MCP server that exposes\nthe Jira-mutating bridge tools, but never provisioned their `acli` transport. This is an omission\nin that originating story's plan (masked until `colourless-hasteless-lamb` wired credentials and\nmoved the probe past its credential gate to the transport). Close class: `plan_defect`.\n\nPlanned fix (Phase 2): add a pinned, arch-aware, sha256-verified `acli` install to\n`Dockerfile.mcp` (build-time download via curl, purged after; installed to `/usr/local/bin/acli`\nwith a `--version` smoke check), plus a manifest test in `tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py`\nasserting the image declares the pinned install (AC #2). No credential value is used at build time."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788022132532309148,"uuid":"9a0f16b1-3090-4f0d-959e-b4ba99d631dd"}